A||||2||wxxo||flex plate question||||1||
Z||000000||wxxo||08-07-2000||10:09 AM||||4 speed manual tranny: which way is the flex plate supposed to face in relation to the flywheel. does the flat side face the flywheel?? (i hope so cause thats the way that i put it in haha.) ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||08-07-2000||11:59 AM||||flex plate in a manual?<BR>Flywheel or clutch plate, flat (supposed to smooth, flat and shiny)faces the transmission side. (torque!) Make sure the clutch disk is installed properly, should have a sticker or stamp that says 'flywheel side'. (remember to use clutch alignment tool!) Be sure to tighten the pressure plate bolts in stages to draw it down evenly to prevent warpage and clutch chatter!||||reg||4
Z||000002||wxxo||08-07-2000||12:13 PM||||well i didnt use an alignment tool (unless you call a socket that fits just right an alignment tool) there is one side on the clutch, flex plate (whatever that disk is that goes between the flywheel and the pressure plate) that is fairly flat and the other side has a raised part in the middle. (btw there was not a stamp on it saying which side was which. i looked for quite some time) i put the side with the raised part in facing the tranny. hope thats the way that its supposed to go cause iv almost got it all back together. i have no business doing a job this big but the shop wanted $2k to do it for me. car isnt worth that much. so thats why i did it myself. learned a lot but i wish that i knew more to begin with. thanks...||||reg||1
